
Direct 1-to-1 Mapping

Spring Boot
@PostMapping("/users")
public User createUser(@RequestBody User user) {
    return userService.save(user);
}

Gin
func CreateUser(c *gin.Context) {
	var user models.User
	c.ShouldBindJSON(&user)
}


✔ Same purpose
✔ Same behavior
✔ Same responsibility

🧠 What ShouldBindJSON actually does

Behind the scenes, Gin:

Reads request body
Parses JSON
Maps JSON → struct fields
Runs validation (if tags exist)
Returns error if invalid

Equivalent to:
HttpMessageConverter + Jackson


Go struct
type User struct {
	Name  string `json:"name"`
	Email string `json:"email"`
}


Gin automatically maps:

name → Name
email → Email



Validation comparison (VERY IMPORTANT)
Spring Boot
public User create(@Valid @RequestBody User user) {}

Gin
type User struct {
	Email string `json:"email" binding:"required,email"`
}

c.ShouldBindJSON(&user)


✔ Same idea
✔ Struct tags replace annotations



| Gin                | Spring           |
| ------------------ | ---------------- |
| `ShouldBindJSON`   | `@RequestBody`   |
| `ShouldBindQuery`  | `@RequestParam`  |
| `ShouldBindUri`    | `@PathVariable`  |
| `ShouldBindHeader` | `@RequestHeader` |
| `ShouldBind`       | Auto detect      |





